16 calls in 2 directories belong to no project. Run `tokendraw projects` to
list them with the labels that would assign them.

Where the energy goes (base case)
  rereading the context               1%
  calls above 200,000 cached tokens   0%
  claude-code / codex / pi            4% / 90% / 6%
  interactive / subagent / headless   84% / 1% / 15%

fixed-context
  Each call re-read on average 4,840 tokens its session or subagent started
  with: the system prompt, tool definitions, instruction files and first
  prompt or brief. That used 80% of the energy.
  What you can do:
    claude-code:
      /context to see what fills the context
      /mcp disable for servers you do not use
      /memory to shorten CLAUDE.md
    codex:
      enabled = false in config.toml for MCP servers you do not use
      shorten AGENTS.md
    pi:
      /mcp to disable servers you do not use
      shorten AGENTS.md
  To see the effect, run this after the change:
  `tokendraw findings --since <tomorrow>`

model-choice
  Subagents and headless runs on models pricier than claude-haiku-5-5
  (claude-code) or gpt-6-luna (codex) used 16% of the energy. On those
  models, the same tokens would have made the total 15% lower.
  What you can do:
    claude-code:
      model: haiku in a subagent's definition
      CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL=haiku
      claude -p --model haiku
      model="haiku" in the Agent SDK's options
    codex:
      agents.default_subagent_model = "gpt-6-luna" in config.toml
      codex exec --model gpt-6-luna
  To see the effect, run this after the change:
  `tokendraw findings --since <tomorrow>`

